Inaccuracies - Modifications

The Sample Project Files and related documentation provided herein could include technical inaccuracies or typographical errors. Changes may be periodically added by RSI to the information herein. RSI and/or its respective licensors and affiliates may make improvements, changes in the materials and/or programs, or remove at will and without prior notice any content described herein at any time. No level of responsibility for accuracy or usability of any content in the Sample Project Files is claimed or accepted.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Initialization_Routine,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Exit_Belt_Speed_Control,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Gearing,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Product_Gap_Generator,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Smart_Belt_Correction,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Product_Gap_Generator" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[SIMULATE A PRODUCT GAP ON THE SMART BELT]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Initiate_Product_Gap_DI4)MAM(Smart_Belt_Axis,Smart_Belt.Product_Gap_MAM,1,Smart_Belt.Product_Gap_Value,50,Units per sec,100,% of Maximum,100,% of Maximum,Trapezoidal,100.0,100.0,% of Time,Disabled,0,0,None,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Smart_Belt_Correction" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This Program Demonstrates a Smart Belt on a (2) Axis K6K (1796-K6K21) demo box.

ENABLE/DISABLE SMART BELT CORRECTION
This rung is used to enable/disable the smart Belt State demo application. It does (2) operations. First, it resets the State Machine Step counter. It also Disarms registration. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(S:FS) ,XIO(Auto_Correction_Enable_DI13) ][MOV(0,Smart.State_Machine) ,[MDW(Smart_Belt_Axis,Smart.Correction_MDR) ,RES(Smart.RegistrationCounter) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ENABLE/DISABLE SMART BELT CORRECTION]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(0,Smart.State_Machine)XIC(Auto_Correction_Enable_DI13)MOV(1,Smart.State_Machine);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ARM REGISTRATION INPUT
This rung arms registration for the Smart Belt Axis. On an actual machine, the Exit Belt Axis position is captured instead of the Smart Belt as shown below. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Smart.State_Machine,1)[MAR(Smart_Belt_Axis,Smart.Correction_MAR,Positive_Edge,Disabled,0,0,1) ,XIC(Smart.Correction_MAR.IP) MOV(2,Smart.State_Machine) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Motion Arm Registration.PC bit becomes true when a package is detected on the Smart Belt. On the K6K demo box, this occurs when the white mark on the motor disk is detected by the registration photoeye. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(2,Smart.State_Machine)XIC(Smart.Correction_MAR.PC)CTU(Smart.RegistrationCounter,?,?)MOV(3,Smart.State_Machine);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The SSV and GSV instructions below are used to obtain the position of the Exit Belt. On an actual machine, this step isn't required since the registration photoeye is wired directly to the Exit Belt Registration Input. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(3,Smart.State_Machine)SSV(AXIS,Exit_Belt_Axis,InterpolationTime,Smart_Belt_Axis.Registration1Time)GSV(AXIS,Exit_Belt_Axis,InterpolatedActualPosition,Smart.Exit_Belt_RegPos)MOV(4,Smart.State_Machine);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CALCULATE SMART BELT REGISTRATION DISTANCE
This rung is used to calculate the Smart Belt correction distance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(4,Smart.State_Machine)[SUB(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegPos,Smart.Exit_Belt_Desired_Reg_Pos,Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw) ,[LES(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,Smart.Half_FlightDistanceMin) ADD(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,Smart.FlightDistance,Smart.Exit_Belt_Reg_Error) ,[GRT(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,Smart.Half_FlightDistanceMax) SUB(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,10,Smart.Exit_Belt_Reg_Error) ,[LIM(Smart.Half_FlightDistanceMin,Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,Smart.Half_FlightDistanceMax) MOV(Smart.Exit_Belt_RegErrRaw,Smart.Exit_Belt_Reg_Error) ,MOV(5,Smart.State_Machine) ] ] ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[SMART BELT CORRECTION MOVE
This rung is used to move the Smart Belt the correction distance calculated above to correrct the product gap.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(5,Smart.State_Machine)[MAM(Smart_Belt_Axis,Smart.Correction_MAM,1,Smart.Exit_Belt_Reg_Error,2.0,Units per sec,100,% of Maximum,100,% of Maximum,Trapezoidal,100.0,100.0,% of Time,Disabled,Current,0,None,0,0) ,XIC(Smart.Correction_MAM.PC) MOV(1,Smart.State_Machine) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
